  <h2 id="rebuilds">Rebuilds</h2>
  <CodeBlock label="output" code={`$ ./build/orca rebuild raw.events 2024-03
rebuild 1
  level 0 clean 2024-03
  level 1 report 2024-03`} />
  <p>
    A rebuild runs every pipeline downstream of a dataset, a
    <a href="/s/orca/docs/build#sensors">sensor</a> or not, over the partitions given.
    Each pipeline is placed at its longest distance from the dataset, so one that reads
    two rebuilt datasets runs after both, and the scheduler queues a level once every run
    before it has succeeded. A run that fails stops the rebuild; resuming it from the UI
    carries on. The rebuild's own commits don't also start the sensors it reruns, so each
    pipeline runs once.
  </p>

